{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Maureen Keane? In you come, I'll do the pressure before Doctor Walsh calls you. Sleeve up for me.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ah sure, I'm grand. Only the routine check, there's not a bother on me. I nearly didn't bother, the parking out there is a disgrace.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): We'll not be long. Sit easy... right, one hundred and fifty eight over ninety two, and the pulse is seventy four. I'll leave it on the screen.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): That's not bad at all. I was legging it in from the car, so the numbers always look worse.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hello Maureen, have a seat. I'm after seeing that reading, one fifty eight over ninety two. You're in for the routine look at the blood pressure and the cholesterol, yeah?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): That's it. Waste of a morning, if you ask me. I feel fine.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Fair enough. How have the tablets been since the last visit?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually, I'm after stopping the cholesterol one. I read a thing online and I said I'd knock it on the head.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Which one was that, the atorvastatin?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, the atorvastatin. I was going to say ten, no, it's the twenty milligrams. Some article, your man saying they do more harm than good, wreck the muscles and the liver. So I stopped.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): And when abouts was that?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Ah I couldn't put a date on it. A few months, maybe after the new year, maybe not. I don't remember.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm not going to give out to you. You read something and you decided. Are you taking anything else for the cholesterol instead?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Not a thing. Sure I'm grand without it.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): And the blood pressure tablet, the ramipril five milligrams?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): I still take that. Only every other day, mind you. Every day seemed a bit much when you're well. The five milligram one, every second day.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): So it was prescribed once a day, and you're taking it every second day. I just want to be clear.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): That's the size of it. And sure my husband Paddy is on the diabetes pills, metformin, five hundred... no, he says a thousand milligrams in the morning. He's forever at me to have one of his. I don't. That's his sugar, not mine.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Good that you don't. Don't start taking his metformin, even the odd tablet. Any chest pain?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not a bit of it.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): What about shortness of breath, walking or sitting?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm, I suppose, sometimes, not really. Nothing I'd bother you with.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'll not put that down as a yes, then. Any swelling of the ankles?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No, the ankles are fine.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Headaches?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Dizziness with the ramipril?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Dizziness? Not at all. Steady as you like.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let me have a listen. Heart sounds are normal, the chest is clear, and there's no swelling at the ankles.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): I told you I'm grand. Are we nearly done? I've bowls on Thursday and I need shoes in town, the old ones are banjaxed.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Nearly there. Let me say it back so we're on the same page. You stopped the atorvastatin twenty milligrams a few months ago after something online. You're still on the ramipril five milligrams, but only every other day. No chest pain, no headache, no dizziness, no swollen ankles. Pressure today is one fifty eight over ninety two. And you don't take Paddy's metformin.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, that's the lot. Don't be making a song and dance of it.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): Grand. What I was going to do is restart the atorvastatin twenty milligrams tonight, and see you again in six months for a routine check.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Ah hold on, before you write anything. I should have said. My brother Jim had a heart attack last year, he was only sixty two. And the last cholesterol, the girl said it was over eight. I left it out because I feel fine.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right. That changes things for me. I won't restart the statin today.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): So what then? I'm still not mad about going back on that yoke.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): We'll repeat the bloods, a cholesterol panel and the kidney function on account of the ramipril, and I'll see you in one month. We'll decide on the statin then, when the numbers are back. Not before.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Bloods. If you insist. I still think I'm fine, but go on.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'd like you to take the ramipril every day, five milligrams, not every second day. Today's pressure is a bit high to be leaving doses out.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Every day? Mm, I suppose. I'll try. No promises, mind.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): Trying is a start. And again, none of Paddy's metformin.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): I heard you. I don't touch them.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (DOCTOR): If you get chest pain, or dizziness that's properly bad, don't sit on it. Come back to us or go to the emergency department.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): There'll be none of that. Honestly.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (DOCTOR): My working impression, and it's only a working one, is that the blood pressure isn't well controlled, partly from taking the ramipril every other day. Where the cholesterol sits, we just don't know since the statin was stopped. The bloods will tell us more.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Sorry for sticking my head in. Will you be wanting anything booked, Doctor?",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yes. Lipids and renal function, and a review visit in one month to revisit the statin. Not the six-month slot.",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Lipids and kidneys I can do Friday morning, Thursday's clinic is full. And I'll put the review in for a month's time.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (PATIENT): Friday suits me better. Thursday is the bowls, I said.",
  "[SEG0050] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Friday at half nine, so. The form will be at reception on your way out.",
  "[SEG0051] person_3 (DOCTOR): Friday for the bloods, and I'll see you in a month, Maureen. We'll talk the statin properly then.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): Right so. Thanks. I'll be grand."
 ],
